    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481-a2">

                <pb facs="0564" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg484"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brodrick to Mr.
                            White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Wak Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear White</hi>: My appeal to Lord Kitchener on
                    behalf of H. M. Wood, now a prisoner of war, has failed, as I feared it
                    would.</p>
                <p>He objects, as was to be expected, to making concessions to men in such a
                    position as Wood’s in contradistinction to those who are our bona-fide
                    enemies.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">St. John
                    Brodrick.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
